      "writtenOn": "2023-03-10T19:20:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we avoid mmap\u0027ing the restricted regions? i thought that is the whole motivation\n\nif gunyah needs the regions to be mmap\u0027d, then it seems like we\u0027ll really need to model more things because we\u0027ll need long term support for\n\n1. hypervisors where all memory is shared (the status quo) or where some memory private but we can bank on crosvm not touching it by accident (pKVM today)\n2. hypervisors where all memory must be mapped, but only some memory is shared and crosvm needs to track the distinction explicitly (needed for gunyah?)\n3. hypervisors where only shared memory is mapped (eventual KVM + memfd_restricted use case)",
