      "writtenOn": "2023-03-13T23:30:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, so in the Android U kernel, gunyah won\u0027t be using restricted_memfd either. crosvm is going to have to continue working with the Android U kernel.\n\nI think your imagining that the real restricted_memfd support in crosvm could be sort of backwards compatible with the older kernels. I\u0027m skeptical of that and also think it would be confusing to have \"restricted_memfd\" code paths that technically don\u0027t use restricted_memfd.\n\nI suggest we name and document things in this CL such that they are distinct from the eventual restricted_memfd support. If we can get lucky, then maybe restricted_memfd can subsume this but it is probably fine if it doesn\u0027t.\n\nI\u0027m leaving some other comments with name and comment ideas, but otherwise no action required for this comment if you agree.",
